{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And they returned from touring the land at the end of forty days.</b> Now is it not four hundred parasangs by four hundred parasangs? And an average person's pace is ten parasangs a day — that is forty days' travel from east to west. And they walked its length and its width? Rather, it was revealed before the Holy One, blessed be He, that He would decree upon them a year for each day, so He shortened the way before them (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:41.982186984Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}